.TH HARMONIC-EXPLORER 1 "June 2026" "harmonic-explorer 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
harmonic-explorer \- explore harmonics, dissonance and chords on a guitar fretboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harmonic-explorer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B harmonic-explorer
opens an interactive tool for understanding why notes sound consonant or
dissonant together, seen through the lens of a guitar fretboard.
.PP
The application offers:
.IP \(bu 2
a clickable guitar fretboard with capo and key selection,
.IP \(bu 2
additive synthesis with selectable waveforms and an ADSR envelope editor,
.IP \(bu 2
live waveform and spectrum visualization,
.IP \(bu 2
a live Plomp\(enLevelt dissonance curve for the selected notes,
.IP \(bu 2
a chord builder with consonance/dissonance analysis of every interval,
.IP \(bu 2
melody playback in the selected key.
.PP
The interface opens in a dedicated WebKitGTK window. If WebKitGTK is not
available, the application falls back to opening in the default web browser
via
.BR xdg-open (1).
Everything runs offline; no network connections are made.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/harmonic-explorer/index.html
The application itself, a self-contained HTML document.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1)
